<%# A native checkbox on the app's tokens.

    It used to carry role="checkbox" and a hard-coded aria-checked="false" on an <input
    type="checkbox">. The role is redundant - a native checkbox already has it - and the static
    aria-checked is worse than redundant: nothing updates it, so once a user ticks the box the
    accessibility tree still says unchecked. Removing both leaves the browser to report the real
    state, which it does correctly.

    It also had data-state="unchecked" with data-[state=checked]:bg-primary styling. data-state is a
    Radix convention and nothing in this app sets it, so those rules never applied - and `primary`
    there is the shadcn near-black navy, not sitf-primary. Under them sat a hidden <span> holding a
    tick SVG and an inline style="pointer-events: none", which nothing ever unhid.

    accent-sitf-primary lets the browser draw the checked state in the brand colour, which is how a
    native checkbox is meant to be tinted. rounded-sm rather than the rounded-lg control token: at
    16px an 8px radius is nearly a circle, and a checkbox reads as a square.

    The 16px box is under WCAG 2.5.8's 24x24 on its own; the associated label is part of the target,
    which is what makes it reachable. Keep the label. %>
<div class="flex items-center gap-2">
  <%= check_box_tag name, "on", false,
                    id: options[:id] || sanitize_to_id(name),
                    class: "size-4 shrink-0 rounded-sm border-slate-300 accent-sitf-primary " \
                           "focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 " \
                           "focus-visible:outline-sitf-primary" %>
  <%= render_label name: name, label: label %>
</div>
